1
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,993
Mr. Matlock, do you wish to rebut?

2
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:12,155
Miss Jenkins,
let me see if I've got this straight.

3
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:14,749
You say that I met with you

4
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:18,230
and told you to give testimony
in this courtroom

5
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,915
that would provide my client
with a false alibi. Is that correct?

6
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:25,390
You told me
that no one would find out.

7
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,788
What else did I tell you?

8
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:32,876
You told me that if I lied,
I would be helping some poor old man.

9
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:38,114
So being a compassionate
Christian woman, I agreed.

10
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:41,113
Oh, so you must be
a student of the Bible.

11
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,829
Yes.

12
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,197
Are you familiar
with a fellow in there named Ananias?

13
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,998
Of course.

14
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:51,197
Would it be fair to say
you patterned your life after him?

15
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:55,518
Well, I guess, after a fashion.

16
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:57,272
Who was Ananias?

17
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:01,752
Well, actually,
I'm more like the Good Samaritan.

18
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,990
Who was Ananias, Miss Jenkins?

19
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,720
Answer the question, please.

20
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:11,518
- I can't. I don't know.
- Then let me educate you.

21
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:15,753
Ananias was the biggest liar
in all antiquity.

22
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:17,795
Defence rests.

23
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:21,589
Sufficient evidence exists
to bind this defendant over for trial.

24
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:25,036
Arraignment is set for Thursday,
26th of the month,

25
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:28,078
9 a.m. in Department 60.

26
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,117
This court is in recess.

27
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,032
- This is a court of law?
- Dad, take it easy.

28
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,918
Can someone explain
what went on here today?

29
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,311
Just a hearing, Mr. Baron. We still
have time to prepare for the trial.

30
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:39,550
I'll be over later.

31
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,910
Follow Alice Jenkins.
Stay on her like a shirt.

32
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:46,150
With pleasure.

33
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,311
Who tipped you off?

34
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:52,116
Gee, my secretary forgot to ask.

35
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,674
<i>He can't take this kind of aggravation,</i>
<i>Mr. Matlock.</i>

36
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,638
He had two heart attacks in prison.
Another could very likely kill him.

37
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:01,994
Have you told him that?

38
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:04,355
In his eyes, I didn't just turn my back
on his business,

39
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,873
I turned my back on him.

40
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,076
That gives him every reason
not to listen to me.

41
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,992
Talk him out of standing trial,
Mr. Matlock,

42
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,913
because if you don't and he dies,

43
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:15,036
you will have killed him.

44
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:29,750
- Well, Nicholas.
- Hello, Ben.

45
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:32,839
My son insists
on keeping me sedated.

46
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:36,118
I think he likes me better that way.

47
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:38,708
Well, Nicholas,

48
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:43,192
like my mother used to say,
''Ain't nothing simple.''

49
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:46,910
Because of your history, I knew
the cards would be stacked against us,

50
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:50,356
but the district attorney's been doing
a better job of stacking than I thought.

51
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:53,799
It's a tough case. Very tough.

52
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,276
What are you trying to say?

53
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:58,749
You don't have to go through
with this trial.

54
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,876
Because of your health,
I can get a postponement.

55
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,837
Probably a slew of them.

56
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,879
You can live out the days you have left
the way they should be lived, in peace.

57
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:10,635
Then people will think
I killed Donald Kovack and Eddie,

58
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,234
and I told you,
I don't wanna die with that on my head.

59
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,311
- All right.
- Now, you said you understood that.

60
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:18,472
You said we had an agreement to see
this through to the end no matter what.

61
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:20,119
All right, all right.

62
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,879
If you don't calm down,

63
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:26,589
I'm gonna get your son in here
and have him turn your lights out.

64
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,391
My son Paul
is more convinced than ever

65
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,710
that you're the wrong lawyer for me.

66
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:35,316
I'm the best lawyer you could hope for,
and I'll tell you why.

67
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:39,595
Whoever's making you look guilty
is making me look bad,

68
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,318
and I don't like that.

69
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,153
It's a matter of honour for me too.

70
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:50,519
Remember, Riverside has priority.
Deliver them first, and then Wildwood.

71
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:51,949
- Hi.
- Hi.

72
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,873
- This is a beautiful place to work.
- It gets hot.

73
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,156
So does a courtroom,
but it doesn't smell as nice.

74
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,548
I can't get over that locket.
It really is unusual.

75
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,949
Thank you. It's Victorian.

76
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,558
My brother is very interested in you,
you know.

77
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:11,392
So he says.

78
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,835
You two don't exactly
seem inseparable.

79
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,436
Well, Paul lets me run this place
as sort of an indulgence.

80
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:21,957
Well, it keeps you off the streets
and out of the kitchen, right?

81
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:24,834
That's one way to look at it.

82
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:31,196
You know,
I lost my mother when I was young.

83
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:35,078
Was it difficult for you?

84
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,236
My father divorced my mother
over 20 years ago.

85
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:41,472
- I barely remember her.
- Where is she now?

86
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,671
When she walked out,
my father forbade any of us

87
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,558
to have any contact with her.

88
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,116
We couldn't write to her or call her.

89
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:52,590
He'd punish us if we so much
as mentioned her name.

90
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:55,515
He even had all the photographs
of her destroyed,

91
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,999
every single one of them.

92
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:59,390
Well, why did she walk out?

93
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,597
My mother loved my father,
but hated what he did.

94
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,035
I guess she thought by marrying him,
she could change him,

95
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,599
but she couldn't.

96
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,876
So she finally left...

97
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,038
...with another man.

98
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,919
My father was outraged.

99
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:17,913
So much so, he even threatened
to have them both killed.

100
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:19,832
My God. What happened?

101
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:24,315
All I know is that somehow,
my brother Daniel stopped him.

102
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,757
How goes it, Tyler?

103
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:45,310
Our friend Alice Jenkins has been in
her apartment for the last three hours.

104
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,269
Probably reading her Bible.

105
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,873
Take a break, I'll hold the fort.

106
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,315
- Get a sandwich or something.
- I'm not hungry.

107
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:54,789
Well, stretch your legs. Take a walk.

108
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,951
Look, that woman
made a fool out of me yesterday,

109
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:00,829
and I don't intend to go anywhere
till I find out what's going on.

110
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,757
You notice anything different
about me?

111
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:09,031
Would you be mad if I don't?

112
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,872
No hay fever.

113
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:15,112
Gone. Dr. Baron cured me.

114
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,748
- Dr. Baron?
- Yeah.

115
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,554
He could be our killer.

116
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,199
Maybe.

117
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:25,591
- You let him stick a needle in you?
- Yeah, you think I made a mistake?

118
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,194
I wouldn't let him stick a needle in me.

119
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:41,350
All right,
both of you come out of there slowly.

120
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:45,391
Any chance they're
talking to somebody in our back seat?

121
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,670
Turn around and put your hands
on the roof of the car.

122
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:53,389
You're making a mistake.
I'm a lawyer, Ben Matlock.

123
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,951
- What's going on?
- We just got a phone call

124
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,839
- telling us about your little drug deal.
- Drug deal?

125
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,991
Yes, drug deal.
Now, where's the rest of the stuff?

126
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,832
That's my medicine.

127
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,833
- All right, search the car.
- Ben, check it out.

128
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,591
Looks like somebody's
going on a trip.

129
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:24,953
- What's the problem here?
- Big drug bust, Harry.

130
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:28,078
They caught me red-handed
with my hay fever medicine.

131
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,798
Take the cuffs off.

132
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,952
Sorry, Mr. Matlock.

133
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:36,673
- You all right?
- Oh, I'm fine. Really swell.

134
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:40,719
Somebody set your boys up so we lost
the most crucial witness in our case,

135
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:42,996
but other than that, things are great.

136
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:51,716
Mr. Johnson, you reside in Atlanta,

137
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,197
and you are a carpenter,
is that correct?

138
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,918
Yes, sir.

139
00:09:57,080 --> 00:10:01,358
Well, you see, we are endeavouring
to empanel a jury to try an indictment

140
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:05,035
against Mr. Nicholas Baron,
who has been charged with the murder

141
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,031
of Edward Alonzo.

142
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,633
Have you read anything about this

143
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:10,711
in the papers or heard about it
on television?

144
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,598
Of course.

145
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:17,153
I've been going over mug shots
all morning and that's our boy.

146
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:20,198
- Roy Vincent.
- Never heard of him.

147
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,475
Any known address?

148
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:25,792
No, but he's got a rap sheet
a mile long, and it's all smalltime stuff.

149
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,837
- I'll find him.
- Yeah, yeah.

150
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:32,357
In the event that you find
the defendant guilty of murder,

151
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,875
would you be reluctant
to return a verdict

152
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:38,794
which would make it mandatory
for the court

153
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,712
to impose the death sentence?

154
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,393
- No, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

155
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:51,072
Have you heard of Nicholas Baron
before this?

156
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,753
Yes, sir.

157
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,597
Do you think you could judge this case
on its own merits

158
00:10:56,760 --> 00:11:00,070
without being influenced
by suppositions and innuendos

159
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,196
you may have heard or read?

160
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,634
I think so, yes.

161
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,589
- Do you know me?
- Not personally.

162
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:11,311
I've defended quite a few cases around
and my name's been in the paper.

163
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:14,074
- You ever heard of me?
- Yes, I have.

164
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,428
What about me, Mr. Johnson?

165
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,591
Do you think the fact
that I'm the defence attorney

166
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,796
might prejudice you in any way?

167
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,713
- It might, yes.
- How's that?

168
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:28,029
I hear you're the kind of lawyer
that gets everybody and his uncle off.

169
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:31,158
Frankly, I'd like to see how you do it.

170
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:35,748
Your Honour, I will accept this juror,
he's obviously honest.

171
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:41,789
Hello.

172
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,549
I don't recall having--

173
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,234
I brought you all the answers
to those questions you gave me.

174
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,278
Take a look.
I think I answered those pretty well.

175
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,670
Yeah. Not that I'm complaining,
but you are a little late,

176
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:54,593
and I think I already have
most of this information.

177
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,990
Actually, it's just an excuse
to come and see you.

178
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,909
How's the case going?

179
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:05,273
- So far it's going nowhere.
- Comes as no surprise to me.

180
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:09,828
- Oh, nice bike. You ride this?
- Yeah, whenever I can.

181
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,116
That's a great idea.

182
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,510
Maybe I ought to buy me one.

183
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:17,240
I don't think they make any
that are bulletproof.

184
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,312
Why are you so hard on me?

185
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,393
You know, we're not so different.

186
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:26,715
No. I went to college,
got an M.B.A., came out,

187
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,996
and I went to business with my father,
just like you.

188
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,515
Yeah, except the business I went into
is legitimate.

189
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,671
Has anyone ever proven
that ours isn't?

190
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:36,229
It's not as if the Justice Department
hasn't tried.

191
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:40,190
Isn't it written somewhere
that you're innocent until proven guilty?

192
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:41,989
Yes.

193
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,674
- Actually, it's written everywhere.
- It is.

194
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:47,832
- Then why doesn't that apply to me?
- Oh, it does.

195
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,150
- Then prove it.
- How?

196
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,550
Dinner tonight. I won't order for you.

197
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,878
And the flowers. I mean, they're lovely,
but please, they gotta stop.

198
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,759
- It's starting to look like a funeral--
- I'll stop sending flowers.

199
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,558
- Eight o'clock.
- Seven thirty.

200
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,119
Seven thirty.

201
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:05,312
Okay.

202
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,030
Okey-doke.

203
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:14,196
Is everything a negotiation with you
or what?

204
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:17,513
What can I say? I'm a lawyer.

205
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,797
I'll call you later.

206
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:24,793
I feel like a new man.

207
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,872
Just a little postnasal drip
in the morning, that's all.

208
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:32,079
Well, the pollen count's
on the way back up.

209
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:36,953
- Another shot would probably help.
- Knew you were gonna say that.

210
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:42,875
What do you hear from your mother?

211
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:44,755
My mother's in California.

212
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:47,388
I know. And I know
at the time of the divorce,

213
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,949
your father forbade the three of you
to communicate with her.

214
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:53,112
I thought he might have
made an exception in your case.

215
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:57,599
- What makes you think that?
- I think I'll wait for the shot to tell you.

216
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,155
I don't know how you did it,

217
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,629
but you kept your father
from killing her, didn't you?

218
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,438
That's none of your business.

219
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:11,077
Under the circumstances,
I'm afraid it is.

220
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:15,199
But it's nothing to be ashamed of.
You saved your mother's life.

221
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:17,358
I know if anybody ever
threatened my mother,

222
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,829
I would have done anything I had to
to stop him.

223
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,835
Of course,
a thing like that's hard to forget,

224
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,673
even harder to forgive.

225
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,110
Ever forgive your father, Daniel?

226
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:32,748
Only God can forgive, Mr. Matlock.

227
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,833
I just try to forget.

228
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:39,191
Thanks for the shot.

229
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,117
Beautiful lawn.

230
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:54,150
- What'd you say?
- I said you got a beautiful lawn.

231
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:58,199
No crabgrass.
That's a big problem out my way.

232
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:01,113
I was thinking about trying
some of that Weed-Away.

233
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:03,999
I hear that'll kill it for keeps.
Did you ever use it?

234
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:05,149
No.

235
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:08,835
Something goes wrong with the lawn,
Mr. Kovack just brings another one in.

236
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:13,956
I can honestly say
that's a solution I never thought of.

237
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:17,510
- Mr. Matlock.
- Hey, Mr. Kovack.

238
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:21,833
I'll be brief. I can see I'm interrupting
your enjoyment of the great outdoors.

239
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,115
Don't worry about it.

240
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:26,593
- Roy Vincent. Do you know him?
- No, why? Who is he?

241
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:29,998
He's a fellow who's seen to it
that a woman who accused me

242
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:33,391
of suborning perjury
is nowhere to be found.

243
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:37,314
I also suspect that somebody
has hired this same fellow

244
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,835
to try to harass me off this case.

245
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,911
Well, it couldn't be
anybody from our family.

246
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:45,470
Like I told you before,
we have identical interests.

247
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:49,713
We just wanna see Nicholas Baron
get what he deserves.

248
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:52,519
Everybody's interested in justice.

249
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:55,513
For a lawyer, that's very,
very encouraging.

250
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,795
That's your brother's widow, isn't it?

251
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:03,829
Seems to be taking his death
pretty hard.

252
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,116
- Anything else, Mr. Matlock?
- No, no.

253
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,555
Oh, yeah, yeah. Congratulations.

254
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:11,837
I hear you officially took over
your brother's business.

255
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,479
Someone had to do it.

256
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,514
That include his home and wife too?

257
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:19,319
- Get out, Mr. Matlock.
- On my way.

258
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:29,033
Laboratory tests
have already confirmed

259
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:32,954
that this gun
was the weapon of death,

260
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:35,918
and it had the fingerprints
of Mr. Nicholas Baron on it.

261
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:38,071
Do you recognise it?

262
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:43,351
Yes, it has my mark on it
and I also tagged this weapon.

263
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,068
Where was it found?

264
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:49,950
The weapon was found approximately
1 5 feet from Mr. Alonzo's body.

265
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,633
Thank you, sir.

266
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,591
Mr. Henderson.

267
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:58,320
Do you recognise this car?

268
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:00,311
Yes, sir, that's the car I saw.

269
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:03,392
And it drove in to the field
next to the man who was digging.

270
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,634
Then what happened?

271
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:09,236
Then the driver leaned over and
fired two shots at him and drove away.

272
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:12,949
- Did you get a look at the driver?
- Yes, I did.

273
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:15,680
- Is he in this courtroom?
- Yes, sir, he is.

274
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:19,150
Would you point him out
to the court, please?

275
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:20,958
That's him.

276
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:26,233
- Are you sure?
- Yes, sir.

277
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:28,469
The record will indicate

278
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:31,837
that the witness
has identified the defendant.

279
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,437
Thank you, Mr. Henderson.

280
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:38,513
Do you wish to ask any questions
for the defence, Mr. Matlock?

281
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:41,717
Yes, Your Honour, but new evidence
has just been brought to my attention.

282
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:44,792
With the court's permission,
I'd like to have a one-hour recess.

283
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:49,315
The court will reconvene
at 2:30 this afternoon.

284
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,278
Charlie, I wanna tell you something.

285
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:54,079
I am in the process
of changing my image.

286
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:58,597
No longer do I want to win
the worst-dressed-man-in-court award.

287
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,875
- You were right.
- What?

288
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:04,113
Matlock is up to something, all right.
Hey, I'll have one of those, please.

289
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:06,909
Would you mind telling me
what it is that he's up to?

290
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,991
Well, I just saw him
hustle four old men

291
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,310
through the backdoor
of the courthouse.

292
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:15,432
Palmer, are you going to come
to the point or not?

293
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:20,196
The point is, they all vaguely resemble
Nicholas Baron.

294
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,273
Charlie, do you have
any cold water--?

295
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:32,238
Will you stay out of this?

296
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:40,513
Now, according to the weather, sir,

297
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:43,433
it was warm and sunny
the morning you went hunting.

298
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,079
Is that--? Does that sound right?

299
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:48,118
- Felt more like hot and sunny.
- Yeah.

300
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:50,396
And what time you say it was
you saw the murder?

301
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:51,595
Right around 8.

302
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:54,594
So it's perfectly clear to the court
where everybody was

303
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,671
in relationship to everything,

304
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:58,831
I've taken the liberty
of drawing this rough sketch

305
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,797
based on your testimony.

306
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:04,475
Now, Point A would be the road,

307
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:09,156
and Point B would be where
Mr. Alonzo fell after he was shot.

308
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,238
And Point C--

309
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:14,198
Would you mind
just stepping down here for a minute?

310
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:15,793
Good.

311
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:21,476
So Point C would be the car
driven by the assailant,

312
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,039
and, D, that would be you.

313
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:24,834
That's right.

314
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:30,233
Now, you say you were 20 or 25 yards
from the car when it stopped.

315
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:33,517
- Twenty, 25 yards, yeah.
- And what direction were you facing?

316
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:36,554
- East.
- East?

317
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:39,676
The sun must have been shining
right in your eyes.

318
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,239
Yeah, it was.

319
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:44,392
It must have been bright.
Too bright to see clearly.

320
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,516
Oh, well, I was wearing sunglasses.

321
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:49,793
Oh, sunglasses.

322
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,792
Like these?

323
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,550
Well, yeah,
mine are sort of like those.

324
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:56,153
Would you put them on
for a moment?

325
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:02,072
Your Honour,
are we going somewhere here?

326
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,559
Your Honour,

327
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:06,029
I am merely trying to recreate
as best I can

328
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:08,998
the conditions under which
this witness saw the shooting.

329
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:12,197
- Proceed, Mr. Matlock.
- All right, thank you.

330
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:15,432
Now, this room
is approximately 20 yards across.

331
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:18,433
Would you turn around
and face the window, please?

332
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:22,720
Now, you say the sun was shining
about like that?

333
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:24,991
- Yeah.
- Okay.

334
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:29,631
I want you to identify the person
you saw driving the Jaguar.

335
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:33,113
Is it one of the two men
in front of the window?

336
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:36,473
No.

337
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,631
Then it's the gentleman
at the defence table.

338
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:41,428
No.

339
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:45,471
The man I saw
is sitting right over there.

340
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:53,109
Indicating the defendant.

341
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:58,669
No further questions.

342
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:03,873
- Call 91 1 .
- Back up, back up.

343
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:12,158
Your Honour, this is just
another one of Mr. Matlock's

344
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:16,279
cheap theatrical tricks designed
to milk sympathy from the jury.

345
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:20,194
Damn it, Jimmy, this is serious.
Somebody call the paramedics.

346
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:38,670
It was another heart attack,
but he's gonna pull through.

347
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,831
He's gonna make it, right?
He's gonna be all right?

348
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,913
- Yeah, Paul.
- Yeah? Okay. All right.

349
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:47,839
He's not going back
into that courtroom, Matlock.

350
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,752
It's too much for him.
I absolutely forbid it.

351
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:52,798
Are you speaking
as his doctor or his son?

352
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,235
For your information,

353
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:00,960
if I wanted revenge for my mother,
I could have taken it just now

354
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:03,714
in that emergency room and no one
would have known the difference.

355
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,872
I've come a long way in 20 years,
and so has he.

356
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:10,075
I'm doing my best to keep him alive,

357
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:13,152
and that means keeping him
out of that courtroom.

358
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:19,268
Mr. Matlock,
is the defence ready to proceed?

359
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:23,076
Your Honour, as you can see,
my client is not present.

360
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:25,913
He is, in fact, in the hospital.

361
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:31,471
Now, my opponent has accused me
of using theatrics.

362
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:36,231
I suggest that he has himself
used quite extraordinary theatrics

363
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:38,595
already in this trial.

364
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:42,954
But if we pursue this honestly,
I'm sure the truth will come out,

365
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:46,430
if indeed that's what
we're all interested in.

366
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,280
I know everybody in this courtroom
has strong feelings

367
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,237
about Nicholas Baron's past,

368
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:55,871
but I submit he is not on trial here
for his past.

369
00:22:56,040 --> 00:23:01,194
He is on trial for the murders
of Donald Kovack and Eddie Alonzo.

370
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:04,831
Defence is aware
that we are entitled to a continuance,

371
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,309
but my client does not want that.

372
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:12,395
He wants this trial to proceed so that
he can be acquitted of these charges

373
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,710
as soon as possible.

374
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:16,996
What does Mr. McShane
say about this?

375
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:21,039
Well, I don't think it matters
if Mr. Baron is here or not.

376
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:23,111
Of course, there are no objections.

377
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:28,195
Very well. We will proceed.
Mr. Matlock, next witness, please.

378
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:30,669
I call Dave Christopher to the stand.

379
00:23:30,840 --> 00:23:34,833
- Ben? Roy Vincent. I tracked him.
- Where is he?

380
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,036
He's holed up in a condominium
out on the east side.

381
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:40,351
The condominium is owned
by none other than Paul Baron.

382
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:46,677
- Have Lieutenant Daniels pick him up.
- You got it.

383
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:58,633
- Have a minute?
- Yeah, sure.

384
00:23:58,800 --> 00:24:02,839
- Just let me talk with the lady.
- We know about you and Roy Vincent.

385
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:04,912
You know what?

386
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:07,232
What's the matter with you?

387
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:12,799
We know about you keeping him.
Using him to try to manipulate us.

388
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:15,155
Trying to scare us.
Well, you scared me, Paul.

389
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:17,356
Didn't you think
we were smart enough to figure it out?

390
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:20,193
- Hey, I think you're mistaken.
- No, I'm not mistaken, Paul.

391
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,952
You were the one
that hired Alice Jenkins,

392
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:24,759
then you tipped off the D.A.,
trying to get us thrown off the case,

393
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:27,229
- maybe even get my father disbarred.
- Charlene, I never--

394
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:29,470
You know what's ironic
about this whole thing?

395
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:32,950
Is that it actually upsets me
that you used me.

396
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:36,112
I hate to admit it,
but it really gets me.

397
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:38,748
Charlene, no matter what,
my feelings for you were always real.

398
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:41,957
No, no. A little late for that, Paul.

399
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:47,069
I mean, tell me,
what is this all about, really?

400
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:49,390
Are you trying to start
some sort of a gangland warfare

401
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,949
between you and the Kovacks
so you can get back into business?

402
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:53,678
- That'll be enough.
- You set us up.

403
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:56,354
Am I to believe that you're incapable
of framing your own father

404
00:24:56,520 --> 00:24:57,635
so that he's out of the way?

405
00:24:57,800 --> 00:25:00,030
- You can stop any time.
- I don't know what to believe.

406
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:01,872
You know, your father is dying.

407
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:04,873
The business would soon be yours,
but maybe you're a bit too impatient,

408
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:07,315
too greedy, and killing two people
is easier than waiting.

409
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:09,277
Let me set you straight
on something.

410
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:11,635
I never wanted your father
on this case,

411
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:14,030
and I never said otherwise.

412
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,711
But I didn't frame my father.

413
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:20,669
And as for you,
you should be very grateful.

414
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:24,510
Because no man could ever say
what you just said to me

415
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:25,999
and get away with it.

416
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:28,192
Come on.

417
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:35,759
Mr. Christopher,
you work for the Kovacks.

418
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:37,990
You work as their gardener.

419
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:39,388
That's right.

420
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:41,437
How'd you end up
in that line of work?

421
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:42,589
What'd you say?

422
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:44,432
How'd you end up
in that line of work?

423
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:46,830
My parole officer recommended it.

424
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:51,232
Oh, that's right, that's right.
You were convicted of a felony.

425
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:53,516
Yeah, a little.

426
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:57,229
A little? More like seven.

427
00:25:57,400 --> 00:26:00,836
Armed robbery, assault,
attempted murder, racketeering.

428
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:04,913
- Objection. Relevancy.
- Objection sustained.

429
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:07,036
When you earned those sentences,

430
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:10,670
were you working for the Kovacks
then as well?

431
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:13,149
I guess you could say
I was working for the Kovacks

432
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:15,117
during those years, yeah.

433
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:18,238
But I'm too old for that stuff now.

434
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:22,109
Oh, so I see. So Donald Kovack
put you on as gardener

435
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:25,352
as a kind of a reward
for all those years of service.

436
00:26:25,520 --> 00:26:27,670
Kind of a retirement plan.

437
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:29,876
I guess you could say that, sure.

438
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:33,157
Are you the only employee
he treats like that?

439
00:26:33,320 --> 00:26:35,356
Oh, no.

440
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:37,511
You got Huey Moore--

441
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:40,638
Convicted murderer,
reputed Mob hit man.

442
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:43,234
Yeah, he does their pool work.

443
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:46,790
- And then you got Vince Jacobs.
- Oh, spent time obstructing justice.

444
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:48,837
Yeah, he does
all their maintenance work.

445
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:51,958
- And then you got Bobby--
- That's enough. That's enough.

446
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:55,317
I'm sure the jury has an idea
of the kind of people

447
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:58,278
who work for Donald Kovack.

448
00:26:58,440 --> 00:27:01,079
Let me ask you something.
Do you have a hearing problem?

449
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:03,710
- What'd you say?
- I said, are you hard of hearing?

450
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:06,519
Yeah, a gun went off next to my ear.

451
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:08,477
By accident.

452
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:12,428
Well, since this witness
is hard of hearing

453
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:15,068
and these next questions
are important,

454
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:17,959
I've taken the liberty
of writing them down.

455
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:23,831
Now, everybody knows
that Nicholas Baron is very ill

456
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,560
and could have gotten this trial
postponed indefinitely,

457
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:28,073
but he didn't do that.

458
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:30,913
So I ask you, if he's guilty,

459
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:35,676
''why would Nicholas Baron
insist on being tried?''

460
00:27:35,840 --> 00:27:39,913
I object, Your Honour. Calls for
speculation on the part of the witness.

461
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:44,870
- Objection sustained.
- Then I'll withdraw that question.

462
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:48,916
Mr. Christopher, in your opinion,

463
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:54,518
is Nicholas Baron
as generous to his old employees

464
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,671
as Donald Kovack is known to be?

465
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:58,273
Oh, yeah. He--

466
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:00,635
Objection. Relevancy, speculation.

467
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,508
Sustained.

468
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:07,879
''Why would Nicholas Baron shoot
his own friend and loyal employee,

469
00:28:08,040 --> 00:28:09,155
Edward Alonzo?''

470
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:11,959
Objection, Your Honour.
Relevancy, speculation.

471
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:15,954
- Lack of foundation.
- Objection sustained.

472
00:28:16,680 --> 00:28:17,908
No further questions.

473
00:28:18,080 --> 00:28:21,516
Thank you, Mr. Christopher.
You've been very helpful.

474
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:29,515
Bailiff, would you pick up
Mr. Matlock's toy?

475
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:33,028
Hello, Dave. How are you?

476
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:38,118
Don't tell me you don't remember me
after all we meant to each other,

477
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:40,191
- David.
- I remember you.

478
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:42,112
Hell, yes, I remember you.

479
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:45,113
The last time we were here,
you were prosecuting me.

480
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:47,794
That's right, that's right.

481
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:50,235
We're on the same side now,
though, aren't we?

482
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:54,154
And we both want the court
to know the truth, don't we?

483
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:55,959
Yeah, sure.

484
00:28:56,120 --> 00:29:01,592
This past year, did you ever serve
as Mr. Kovack's driver?

485
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,150
- Yeah.
- And did you happen to drive him

486
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:10,269
to Hilton Head, South Carolina,
on the weekend of March the 1 5th?

487
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:18,149
Hey, David, you wouldn't want me
to have to send you back to prison

488
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:21,073
on something as silly as perjury,
would you?

489
00:29:22,440 --> 00:29:25,637
No. No, I drove him to Hilton Head
a couple of times.

490
00:29:25,800 --> 00:29:27,836
But I don't remember the dates.

491
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,753
Oh, well, then, let me help you on that,
if I may.

492
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:34,071
On that particular date,
he took a guest.

493
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:38,269
Do you remember
who the guest was?

494
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:41,000
- Dave.
- Yeah.

495
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:46,117
- I remember.
- And is that person in the courtroom?

496
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:47,869
Yeah.

497
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:51,157
Would you point that person out,
please?

498
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,668
The lady in the front row
with the dark grey dress on

499
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:57,239
and the long brown hair.

500
00:29:57,400 --> 00:30:02,269
May the record show that the witness
has identified Miss Cathy Baron,

501
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:04,431
the defendant's daughter.

502
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,876
Objection, Your Honour.
Totally irrelevant.

503
00:30:08,040 --> 00:30:12,158
On the contrary, Your Honour.
This liaison provides further motive

504
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:15,198
for the defendant
to order Donald Kovack's murder.

505
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:17,432
Objection overruled.

506
00:30:17,600 --> 00:30:21,878
The record will indicate the witness
has identified Miss Cathy Baron.

507
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:25,030
Thank you, Your Honour.
No further questions.

508
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:26,758
Then this court is adjourned.

509
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:29,798
It will reconvene
on Monday at 9 a.m.

510
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:40,954
It's true. We were having an affair,
but I loved him.

511
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:44,192
I want you to find who killed him,
Mr. Matlock.

512
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:47,275
I wanna see him pay.

513
00:30:57,280 --> 00:30:59,350
I should have seen it coming.

514
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,309
- I should have seen it coming.
- Oh, Dad, look,

515
00:31:02,480 --> 00:31:04,835
it was such a curve
that Wally Joyner couldn't have seen it.

516
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:07,036
How did the DA find out?
That's what I can't figure.

517
00:31:07,200 --> 00:31:10,192
Are you kidding?
Another call from Deep Throat.

518
00:31:10,360 --> 00:31:12,749
Paul Baron's probably got
the DA's number on automatic redial.

519
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:15,229
You can certainly bet
that he's got his sec--

520
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:20,790
I got something
you might want a copy of.

521
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:24,350
Something I'll be filing first thing
Monday morning on my father's behalf.

522
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:26,877
He's removing you as counsel.

523
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:28,959
You're off the case.

524
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,149
Cup of coffee, Tony?

525
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:57,515
Thank you, Ben. Listen,
don't tell me you've been towed.

526
00:31:57,680 --> 00:32:00,148
No, I'd just like to take a look
at the Baron car if it's okay.

527
00:32:00,320 --> 00:32:02,117
- Sure enough.
- Yeah.

528
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:05,434
No donuts today, huh, Ben?

529
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:09,672
- You and Helen find a house yet?
- No, no, we're still looking.

530
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:12,912
- It's a big decision, you know.
- It won't get any smaller.

531
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:14,911
Neither will that waistline
with those donuts.

532
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:17,878
Well, listen,
it's hard to give up donuts, Ben.

533
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:21,956
It's a beautiful car.
I bet it runs like a top.

534
00:32:22,120 --> 00:32:24,475
Yeah, with the price tag they put on it,
it ought to.

535
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:26,119
Yeah.

536
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:28,869
My mother knew a fellow
who had a car like this once.

537
00:32:29,040 --> 00:32:31,508
Said he did nothing
but worry about it.

538
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:33,989
Take him nearly all day
to find a place to park it.

539
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,958
Couldn't park it in the shade
because of birds,

540
00:32:37,120 --> 00:32:39,190
couldn't park it next to other cars
because of nicks,

541
00:32:39,360 --> 00:32:41,669
couldn't park it in the sun
because of the upholstery.

542
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:46,114
Beautiful as it was, for as long as he
had it, it was the bane of his existence.

543
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:49,477
- Did he sell it?
- No, somebody stole it.

544
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:01,433
- Beautiful car, though, huh?
- Oh yeah.

545
00:33:01,920 --> 00:33:03,558
Tell you what.

546
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:08,273
When this is over, maybe we'll talk
the Baron into taking us a ride.

547
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:11,080
Don't wanna hurt your feelings,
but I ain't gonna hold my breath.

548
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:12,639
Interesting idea, though.

549
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:15,189
Cop taking a nice Sunday afternoon
drive with the Baron,

550
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:19,478
talking about people's barns
and orchards, having donuts.

551
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:21,756
Oh, go on, you.

552
00:33:24,120 --> 00:33:26,190
Tell you one thing, Charlene.

553
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:29,158
Nicholas Baron never visited
Edward Alonzo in this apartment.

554
00:33:29,320 --> 00:33:31,993
He would have died two floors ago.

555
00:33:37,800 --> 00:33:40,314
I thought you said
we were off the case.

556
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,598
Well...

557
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:47,393
...they can't file a real substitution
till Monday.

558
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:53,908
Somebody paid that man $25,000
to kill Donald Kovack.

559
00:33:54,480 --> 00:34:00,191
It seems to me the best place
to transact that kind of business

560
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:02,920
would be right here
in this apartment.

561
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:06,233
Dad, look at this.

562
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:09,310
Pictures of Nicholas' children
when they were little.

563
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:11,994
There's Cathy, there's Paul.

564
00:34:12,640 --> 00:34:14,471
Alonzo really was
like a second father to them.

565
00:34:14,640 --> 00:34:17,200
He's got a whole family album here.

566
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:20,352
Wait a sec. This is odd.

567
00:34:20,520 --> 00:34:24,274
Judging from her clothes,
it looks like it might be the mid-'60s.

568
00:34:25,040 --> 00:34:26,712
Guess who?

569
00:34:26,880 --> 00:34:29,394
Think it might be
the former Mrs. Baron?

570
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:31,118
Could be.

571
00:34:32,440 --> 00:34:34,158
Dad.

572
00:34:35,200 --> 00:34:37,395
Look at the strange way
this has been cut out.

573
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:42,513
Yeah.

574
00:34:49,480 --> 00:34:51,436
- Mr. Matlock.
- Good morning.

575
00:34:51,600 --> 00:34:53,636
I just dropped by to see Nicholas
if it's all right.

576
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:56,792
Nobody just drops by on us,
Mr. Matlock.

577
00:34:56,960 --> 00:35:00,157
- Maybe I'm presenting my bill.
- Well, maybe you should just mail it.

578
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:01,355
Look.

579
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,910
Don't make me throw you
out of this house.

580
00:35:04,800 --> 00:35:06,916
I'm counting on three things here.

581
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:11,473
First, your goons are not in the habit
of throwing men my age around.

582
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:14,473
Second, you're not in the habit
of calling the police.

583
00:35:14,640 --> 00:35:19,350
Third, you're just dying to know if I've
found out something you should know.

584
00:35:19,520 --> 00:35:21,078
Excuse me.

585
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:39,517
That's right, I'm still here.
Holding up my end of the deal.

586
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:42,549
You had my word.
I thought I had yours.

587
00:35:43,520 --> 00:35:44,999
What do you want?

588
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,552
Look at this.

589
00:35:57,680 --> 00:35:58,908
No.

590
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:01,675
It isn't possible.

591
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:06,032
- It isn't possible.
- I'm afraid it is.

592
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:07,952
What are you gonna do with this?

593
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:10,270
Nicholas,
I have to do something with it.

594
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:12,717
- I won't allow it.
- Nicholas--

595
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:14,950
I won't allow it.

596
00:36:15,600 --> 00:36:18,751
I know how difficult
this is gonna be for you.

597
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:22,796
But remember,
no matter how it turns out,

598
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:26,191
it might turn out to be
what neither of us wanted.

599
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:28,635
But that was our deal,
and like it or not,

600
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:30,631
I'm gonna have to hold you to it.

601
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:34,951
I'm gonna go ahead with it.

602
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:44,437
This court is now in session.
Honourable Irene Sawyer presiding.

603
00:36:44,600 --> 00:36:46,158
Be seated.

604
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:48,470
The defence may proceed.

605
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:51,757
I call as my next witness...

606
00:36:53,080 --> 00:36:54,638
May I have a moment
with my client?

607
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:56,552
Make it brief, Mr. Matlock.

608
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:01,792
- You shouldn't be here.
- I've told him.

609
00:37:01,960 --> 00:37:03,871
I'm here, Matlock. Get on with it.

610
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:12,630
I call as my next witness
Catherine Baron.

611
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:17,591
Miss Baron, you were having
an affair with Donald Kovack?

612
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:18,749
Yes.

613
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:21,878
Was that affair going on
at the time of his death?

614
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:23,234
Yes.

615
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:25,311
Donald Kovack was a married man,
wasn't he?

616
00:37:26,080 --> 00:37:28,833
- He was going to leave his wife.
- When?

617
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:32,912
- Eventually.
- Were you getting impatient?

618
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:34,959
No.

619
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,950
Did you ever drive
in your father's car?

620
00:37:39,120 --> 00:37:41,475
- No.
- Not ever?

621
00:37:42,160 --> 00:37:46,119
- Never.
- Interesting thing about that car.

622
00:37:46,920 --> 00:37:51,675
I went out to the impound lot
over the weekend to look it over,

623
00:37:52,640 --> 00:37:57,634
and the driver's seat
was moved all the way forward.

624
00:37:58,240 --> 00:38:01,630
All the way.
Now, your father is as tall as I am,

625
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:04,473
which means that
whoever drove that car last

626
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:06,710
had to be a lot smaller.

627
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:09,157
Maybe even your size.

628
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:11,193
Wasn't me.

629
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:13,635
So you have no idea
why the seat was all the way forward?

630
00:38:14,240 --> 00:38:15,639
No.

631
00:38:18,040 --> 00:38:22,431
I understand Eddie Alonzo
was an old friend of the family.

632
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:27,028
- Did you keep track of him?
- I haven't seen him in years.

633
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:30,994
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

634
00:38:31,440 --> 00:38:35,956
You took $25,000
out of your trust fund

635
00:38:36,120 --> 00:38:43,913
the same week that Eddie Alonzo
put $25,000 down on a house.

636
00:38:46,320 --> 00:38:49,153
You think that's just a coincidence?

637
00:38:49,680 --> 00:38:51,477
I suppose so.

638
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:54,918
You know,

639
00:38:56,200 --> 00:38:58,998
I've been meaning to tell you

640
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:04,116
that locket you always wear
is beautiful.

641
00:39:06,080 --> 00:39:09,789
- Thank you.
- My mother had one something like it.

642
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:13,589
You open it up
and there's pictures inside.

643
00:39:14,080 --> 00:39:15,433
Does yours open up?

644
00:39:17,040 --> 00:39:19,031
Does yours open up?

645
00:39:20,520 --> 00:39:23,512
- Yes.
- Would you open it, please?

646
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:28,198
That's private.

647
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:31,238
Stop. I confess, I did it.
I killed them both.

648
00:39:31,400 --> 00:39:34,710
Please, stop, stop, stop.
Please, please.

649
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:38,075
Stop, please, please.

650
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:39,593
It's too late.

651
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:43,548
Would you like some time
with your client, Mr. Matlock?

652
00:39:43,720 --> 00:39:45,472
No, Your Honour.

653
00:39:46,680 --> 00:39:49,240
We apologise for the outburst.

654
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,791
You may proceed.

655
00:39:57,240 --> 00:40:00,949
Your father just confessed
to murders he didn't commit.

656
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:03,270
Would you open the locket, please?

657
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:18,278
Very pretty.

658
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:20,154
Your mother?

659
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:25,957
I didn't know any pictures
of her existed. Where did you get it?

660
00:40:27,400 --> 00:40:29,789
I can't remember.

661
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:38,589
That picture came...

662
00:40:40,160 --> 00:40:42,469
...from this photo album.

663
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,631
From that picture.

664
00:40:48,240 --> 00:40:50,834
This photo album
belonged to Eddie Alonzo.

665
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:53,116
It came from his apartment.

666
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:57,353
Isn't it true that Eddie Alonzo
cut that picture out and gave it to you

667
00:40:57,520 --> 00:41:00,876
when you came to him
with the $25,000?

668
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:02,075
Isn't it true you told him

669
00:41:02,240 --> 00:41:04,959
you wanted to avenge
your father's wrongful imprisonment,

670
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:06,872
when in fact you wanted
to avenge yourself

671
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:08,792
on a man who
wouldn't leave his wife for you?

672
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:13,033
Isn't it true that you gave Eddie Alonzo
$25,000 to kill Donald Kovack?

673
00:41:13,200 --> 00:41:15,634
And isn't it true
that you took your father's car

674
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:18,519
and gun and went to the field
where you knew Eddie would be

675
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:20,477
and shot him?

676
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:23,711
Isn't all of that true?

677
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:25,998
Yes.

678
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:28,072
Yes.

679
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:33,399
Yes.

680
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:42,958
Your Honour,

681
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:45,755
due to the testimony of this witness,

682
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:49,754
the people will at this time
move to dismiss the case

683
00:41:49,920 --> 00:41:51,831
against Nicholas Baron.

684
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:54,673
On motion of the people,
the case is dismissed.

685
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:56,068
Court is adjourned.

686
00:42:06,960 --> 00:42:09,838
Miss Baron, I'm afraid you're gonna
have to come with me, please.

687
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:12,639
Frank, her father would like
to have a word with her.

688
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:14,392
What do you say?

689
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:18,879
Congratulations, Matlock.

690
00:42:19,040 --> 00:42:23,079
- If I ever need a lawyer...
- I think I'll be unavailable.

691
00:42:26,520 --> 00:42:30,115
Well, Ben, I gotta admit it.
You did a hell of a fine job.

692
00:42:30,280 --> 00:42:32,111
How's that?

693
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:33,829
You heard me.

694
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:36,673
I did give you a pretty good fight,
though, didn't I?

695
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:39,195
You gave me some sharp jabs.

696
00:42:39,360 --> 00:42:42,272
- Just like old times?
- Just like old times.

697
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:57,678
Cathy.

698
00:42:58,600 --> 00:43:00,716
You wanted to see me?

699
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:03,919
Yes.

700
00:43:04,960 --> 00:43:08,316
Why? You never wanted
to talk to me before.

701
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:10,391
I'm sorry, Cathy.

702
00:43:10,560 --> 00:43:13,552
I'm sorry you've hated me
all these years.

703
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,672
I'm sorry about your mother.

704
00:43:17,040 --> 00:43:22,319
I may not have pulled the trigger,
but I accept some of the responsibility.

705
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:25,876
I'm sorry, Cathy.

706
00:43:30,960 --> 00:43:32,188
Daddy.

707
00:43:44,360 --> 00:43:45,952
Considering your ties
to organised crime,

708
00:43:46,120 --> 00:43:47,678
how does this affect your family?

709
00:43:47,840 --> 00:43:50,035
- No comment.
- Mr. Baron...

710
00:43:50,480 --> 00:43:52,311
No comment.
That's enough questions. That's it.

711
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:54,550
No more questions.
I said no more questions.

712
00:43:54,720 --> 00:43:56,358
Have you seen your sister?

713
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:06,715
I learned one very important lesson.

714
00:44:06,880 --> 00:44:08,791
I hope so.

715
00:44:10,880 --> 00:44:13,269
Always hire a smart lawyer.

716
00:44:15,440 --> 00:44:17,032
Goodbye, Paul.

717
00:44:25,560 --> 00:44:27,790
- You okay?
- Yeah.

718
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:41,437
You were right, Matlock.

719
00:44:41,920 --> 00:44:43,148
Too little...

720
00:44:43,960 --> 00:44:45,678
...too late.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
